# uninstall removes an installed program and refuses a directory as the
# target.
exec aigw uninstall --help
cmp stdout help.txt

exec aigw install --target $WORK/bin/aigw$exe
exec aigw uninstall --target $WORK/bin/aigw$exe
cmp stdout removed.txt
! exists $WORK/bin/aigw$exe

exitcode 1 aigw uninstall --target $WORK
normalize stdout refusal.out
cmp refusal.out refusal.txt

-- help.txt --
AIGW  aigw uninstall
────────────────────────────────────────
  Withdraw AIGW-owned client projections, then remove the portable
  executable and its rollback copy. This retains Account and Route data
  and stored Tokens. Homebrew-managed copies must be removed with
  Homebrew; this command does not manage them.

Usage
  aigw uninstall [flags]

Options
  -h, --help            help for uninstall
      --target string   installed executable path; defaults to the running executable
-- removed.txt --
AIGW  Portable uninstall
────────────────────────────────────────
  ✓ Removed AIGW client projections, executable, and its single rollback copy
  Configuration and credential-store secrets were preserved.
  Versioned credential readers were retained for cached or other-installation callers.
-- refusal.txt --
AIGW  Action required
────────────────────────────────────────

Problem
  Portable program removal is incomplete

Evidence
  AIGW could not remove every selected portable program file.

Impact
  No AIGW configuration existed; no managed client withdrawal was needed. Tokens and versioned credential readers are retained.

Recommended action
  Inspect the selected target and retained files; after resolving file access, retry `uninstall --target <path>` from another verified AIGW executable.
